{"causes": ["The ongoing Imeretian Civil Wars created a power vacuum that ambitious regional princes like Demetrius sought to exploit.", "The weak central authority in both Guria and Imereti allowed powerful noble families to frequently depose and install rulers.", "The broader geopolitical rivalry between the Ottoman and Safavid Empires fueled internal Georgian conflicts by supporting various factions."], "effects": ["Demetrius's brief rule further destabilized the Kingdom of Imereti, prolonging the civil wars and power struggles.", "His blinding in 1664 served as a harsh political deterrent against future usurpations of the Imeretian throne.", "The Gurieli dynasty's attempts to expand influence into Imereti contributed to the long-term fragmentation of western Georgian polities."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "demetrius-of-guria", "sourceName": "Demetrius of Guria", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "imeretian-civil-wars", "targetName": "Imeretian Civil Wars", "context": "Demetrius of Guria actively participated in the Imeretian Civil Wars, briefly seizing the throne in 1663."}, {"sourceSlug": "demetrius-of-guria", "sourceName": "Demetrius of Guria", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "guria-principality", "targetName": "Guria Principality", "context": "Demetrius of Guria served as the Prince of Guria from 1658 to 1668, exercising his primary rule within the principality."}, {"sourceSlug": "house-of-gurieli", "sourceName": "House of Gurieli", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "demetrius-of-guria", "targetName": "Demetrius of Guria", "context": "Demetrius of Guria was a member of the House of Gurieli, the ruling dynasty of the Principality of Guria."}, {"sourceSlug": "ottoman-safavid-rivalry", "sourceName": "Ottoman-Safavid Rivalry", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "demetrius-of-guria", "targetName": "Demetrius of Guria", "context": "The broader Ottoman-Safavid rivalry significantly influenced the political landscape and power struggles that Demetri